# PRAETOR -- open-source hygiene

# Python build artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# PRAETOR's own report outputs
praetor-report.txt
praetor-report.json
praetor-out/

# Generated test corpus.
# The vulnerable fixtures contain realistic secret-SHAPED tokens and injection
# payloads (all fake -- see references/test-corpus/README.md). Committing them
# would trip other teams' secret scanners / GitHub push-protection and pollute
# history. We ship ONLY the generator; regenerate locally with:
#     python references/test-corpus/_generate_corpus.py
references/test-corpus/vulnerable/
references/test-corpus/clean/

# Claude Code harness state (session locks, scheduled-task bookkeeping). Not source.
# Kept out deliberately: a blind `git add -A` would otherwise commit session state
# into this repo.
.claude/

# Python build artifacts
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Rust build artifacts (the port -- see references/ADR-001-engine-language.md).
# NOT `target/` unanchored: that would also swallow any future directory named
# `target` elsewhere in the tree, and this repo ships a scanner whose own test
# corpus uses arbitrary directory names.
/rust/target/

# Cargo.lock IS committed on purpose -- this workspace ships a binary, and a
# security tool's users should be able to reproduce the exact dependency set
# that was audited. (Libraries conventionally omit it; applications do not.)
